{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>You shall not make yourselves abominable.</b> Because they are defiled and foul." "<b>And you shall not defile yourselves in them</b> — for it is known that the body that is eaten turns into flesh in the body of the one who eats:" "<b>ונטמתם בם.</b> Defective alef, like מראשית without the second alef. And some say they are two roots, the proof being נטמינו בעיניכם, and its meaning is like a person who has no understanding:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:39.491448367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}